her a MATERIAL deviation nor finely balanced evidence — and even if consulted the citable counters show no pattern (0 deviation flags in 90 days; 0 of 350 completed trips). The chat log holds 0 messages, so no rider-requested detour under POL-RD-04 can be shown, waypoint_hint is absent, and no pickup or dropoff amendment under POL-RD-05 exists. The only traffic advisory in the bundle, EV-ADVIS-02807-01, is MISSING at weight_multiplier 0.0 with issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT; the driver has not asserted an external traffic cause, so the missing advisory carries nothing and, under POL-RD-13, engages no POL-RD-10(5) escalation. No POL-RD-10 trigger fires at all: the three artifacts all carry trip TRP-02807, the trace is unimpaired, the timestamps agree, no charge line is unmatched, and the refund computed is nil and far below the 150.00 ceiling. Nor is any driver compensation due under POL-RD-04: the fare was billed on 16.9 km against a trace of 16.91 km, a shortfall of 0.01 km, well under the 1.0 km threshold. The outcome is NO_ACTION, which under POL-GEN-03 is party-relative: this dispute was filed by the rider, payment_status is CHARGED with refund_issued_sgd 0.00, and the metered fare of 23.44 stands as collected. No money moves, so nothing is held for execution under POL-GEN-05. One claim advanced on the rider's behalf was discarded before I ruled — it cited the missing advisory without naming its issue codes, which POL-GEN-02(1) requires; it is recorded in the audit trail below. The driver's statement that he followed the navigation is not relied on either way: the outcome rests on the measured trace and the clause threshold, not on his account or on any excuse. Confidence is 0.95, above the 0.70 floor; the deciding facts (trace distance 16.91 km and booked optimal 15.1 km) are carried by EV-GPS-02807 and EV-TRIP-02807, both at full weight 1.0. This ruling is provisional and may be appealed once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04."
