der POL-RD-04 exists; pickup_amended_at, dropoff_amended_at and amended_optimal_distance_km are all null, so POL-RD-05 cannot be run; and EV-ADVIS-02807-01 is MISSING, carries weight 0.0 and fires issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, so its absence cannot support a POL-RD-03 exoneration for a closure no record describes. Neither party invoked that absent advisory as an excuse, so POL-RD-10(5) is not engaged by it; the absence is a gap in the bundle, not a contradiction in it. The driver's statement that he followed the navigation cites no evidence ID and asserts no external traffic cause; under POL-RD-08 it carries no weight either way, and it does not move the arithmetic.\n\nNo escalation trigger fires: the trip identifiers match across trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown; the trace is unimpaired so POL-RD-10(3) is not engaged; no timestamps disagree by more than 10 minutes or run backwards; no charge line lacks a counterpart; and no two admissible sides are in contradictory evidence of comparable strength. This is an ordinary sub-threshold case, decided on the merits rather than held. The POL-RD-06 driver-profile check is not reached — there is no material deviation, and in any event driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 (below 3) and 0 divided by completed_trips_90d of 350 is 0.00 (below 0.05) — so no conduct referral is produced, and no other clause produces a referral on these facts.\n\nOutcome: NO_ACTION. The metered fare of SGD 23.44 stands as charged; no amount is refunded to the rider and no compensation is paid to the driver. The monetary effect is nil, below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so nothing is held. Confidence is 0.95, resting on the GPS trace and the trip record, both at weight 1.0."
